From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zack Siri
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:08:43 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] Install rtkit so PipeWire gets realtime priority

PipeWire requests realtime scheduling from RealtimeKit at startup, but
rtkit is not a dependency of Arch's pipewire packages and no rlimits
fallback is configured either. On a stock install every data-loop thread
runs at SCHED_OTHER nice 0, so audio produces xruns and crackling under
sustained CPU/GPU load (gaming, GPU inference, compilation).

Ship rtkit in the base package list, and repair existing installs with a
migration that installs it and restarts the running audio units so the
priority request succeeds without a reboot.

Fixes #9390

Upstream: omacom/omarchy#12428
Backport-of: c906004781964cf0575b404e88d5d15872363aa4

(cherry picked from commit c906004781964cf0575b404e88d5d15872363aa4)
---
 install/omarchy-other.packages |  1 +
 migrations/1789747667.sh       | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 migrations/1789747667.sh

diff --git a/install/omarchy-other.packages b/install/omarchy-other.packages
index 7183ac3c..a3edbf42 100644
--- a/install/omarchy-other.packages
+++ b/install/omarchy-other.packages
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ pipewire-jack
 pipewire-libcamera
 pipewire-pulse
 qt6-wayland
+rtkit
 snapper
 sof-firmware
 thermald
diff --git a/migrations/1789747667.sh b/migrations/1789747667.sh
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..dac3cfca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/migrations/1789747667.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+echo "Install rtkit so PipeWire gets realtime priority"
+
+# PipeWire requests realtime scheduling via RealtimeKit at startup, but rtkit
+# is not a dependency of Arch's pipewire packages and the rlimits fallback is
+# not configured either (see https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/issues/9390).
+# Without it, audio threads run at SCHED_OTHER nice 0 and produce xruns under
+# sustained load.
+omarchy-pkg-add rtkit
+
+# rtkit only takes effect when PipeWire re-requests priority at startup.
+# Restart the audio units if they are running; harmless when idle or as root.
+systemctl --user try-restart pipewire.service pipewire-pulse.service wireplumber.service 2>/dev/null || true
